WEBVTT

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:24.950
That night, Mayuko, a fellow club member, passed this area on her way home from her viola lesson.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.960
Please...

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.510
Do you think the ghost I saw was the same one Mayuko saw?

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.780
Probably.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.060
Hey.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.460
I was looking for you.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.520
What are you doing here?

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:22.050
I was asking how this simpleton ended up in Doctor Kinoshita's clinic.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:25.820
Simpleton? Don't call me that! You make me seem like an idiot!

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.540
I heard someone saved you from the river after you fell in and took you to that clinic.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.350
How did you manage to fall in?

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.290
My friend asked me to-

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.790
Drown in the river?

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.020
No, of course not.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.540
She told me that she saw a ghost around here.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.300
I decided to investigate, but ended up falling in the river instead.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.730
You should really leave such things to Yakumo.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:50.930
But...

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.940
I don't want to be someone who just uses Yakumo-kun for his powers.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.370
I see.

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:12.450
She has the same name as your sister.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.250
If something were to happen to you, I wouldn't be able to face her.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.460
So, the next time something like this happens, just come to me.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.400
Yakumo-kun...

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.710
Otherwise, I'll only have more problems further down the road.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:28.730
Geez...

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.220
You always say too much.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.740
First, I need to apologize to you, Doctor.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.240
I'm not a police officer.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.450
I'm just an ordinary university student.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.490
Why did you lie about that?

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.050
What I'm about to tell you will sound like a joke, but it isn't.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.100
A woman's been possessed by a ghost.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:02.750
I asked him for his help.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:06.510
I can see ghosts with my left eye.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.760
And our investigation has led us here.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:20.280
The woman has been possessed by the ghost of Ando Takashi.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.530
We found this in his personal effects.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.190
Do you know anything about it?

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.540
I read in the papers that Ando-kun had died.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.720
Did you know him?

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.920
He was my junior in medical school.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.290
We kept in touch even after I graduated.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.480
He was a kind man.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.660
He was worried about us. After my wife died, my daughter and I became depressed.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.800
I was aware that there were many bad rumors surrounding him...

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.800
but he was someone important to both Ayaka and I.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.870
I had this photograph developed for him after my daughter died.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.390
He asked if he could have a picture of her to remember her by.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:01.310
How did Ayaka-san die?

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.940
It happened a year ago.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.110
There was a typhoon that day...

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.460
On her way home from cram school,

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.820
she accidentally fell into the swollen river, and...

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.330
I met Ayaka-san's ghost a while ago.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:27.340
Her ghost is still lingering around the area and is constantly begging people to "Stop it."

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.470
Do you know why she would say that?

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.340
No, I don't...

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:38.850
Doctor, are you by any chance trying to resurrect Ayaka-san?

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.360
It's a natural wish to have, isn't it?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.860
I guess all we have is whatever leads we get with the keys.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:55.950
Keys?

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.370
They were part of Ando's personal effects.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.190
There's another just like that.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.340
Ishii's looking into that one.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.160
Th-This is...

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:20.890
Please stop the car.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.160
What's wrong with you all of a sudden?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.690
Please take a look at that.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.900
What?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.060
What the hell are you talking about?

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.370
I see that you're as slow as always,

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.680
and that's exactly why your wife left you.

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:41.500
It's the same lettering that's written on the key.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.280
Haruka-chan, stay here.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.170
Please be careful.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:50.010
Idiot! You're coming with me.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.660
Hey, do you sense that?

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.210
Indeed. I sense the presence of another human.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.710
Progress has been made in the investigation.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:39.220
Hashimoto Rumi-san, who went missing, has been safely found.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:42.510
Hashimoto Rumi-san has been taken to the hospital.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.670
She suffered no serious injuries.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:49.230
According to the statement she gave us, Ando did not rape her.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:53.030
Furthermore, we found personal effects belonging to each of the murdered girls at the scene.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:53.950
Is that so?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.870
Return to your posts.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:05.250
It appears the deceased Ando was behind the serial kidnapping and murder incidents.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.390
That means the case is closed now, right?

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:11.680
But that doesn't solve our problem.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:17.830
Yeah, we're nowhere near solving that journalist's problem.

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:35.280
Hello, Nao-chan.

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:37.910
It's been a while, Haruka-chan.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.170
Yes it has, Isshin-san.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.120
What are you doing here?

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:48.010
I came here hoping to ease the suffering of the ghosts of those who died here as much as I could.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:53.300
And since I happened to be in the area, I came to say hello to her.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.180
I see...

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:59.600
Ayaka-san's father saved my life.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.300
I'm on my way to thank him.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:05.200
That's a great idea.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.310
Oh?

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.310
Ah, this?

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:14.810
Yakumo-kun asked me to hold on to it for him.

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.000
So...

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:22.680
Yakumo's mother, Azusa, is my only sister.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:30.330
Can I also ask you to hold on to that until she comes back?

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:32.740
Of course.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:37.840
My invitation was for Yakumo-kun only.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.230
Just get on with it and tell us.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.120
Oh, that's right. Where's Ishii-san?

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.590
Don't mention his name in front of me.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.100
Whatever.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:52.580
These are photographs of each of the victims' faces from the serial kidnapping and murder incidents.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:56.470
I took them at the site for personal use.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.420
You perverted geezer.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.610
I'm diligent in my work, aren't I?

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.610
This is...

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.580
I've been doing this job for a long time,

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:13.000
but this is the first time in my career that I've seen such peaceful expressions on victims.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:16.740
I'd like to hear your opinion.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.770
Hey, Yakumo, look at this.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.900
I never imagined that you'd come all this way just to thank me.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:46.410
Am I intruding?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.890
No, not at all.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.410
In fact, I was planning to call you myself.

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.920
Since I really needed to see you again. No matter what.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.760
I'm not quite sure I'm following... this?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.920
<i>He</i> told me...

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:09.600
that you're worthy of being a vessel for my daughter's soul.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:27.210
Anyway, now that we know he's involved, we've got no time to waste.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:30.730
I don't care if he's a suspect in a different case. We need to question Kinoshita.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:42.340
Tonight, your precious friend will die.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:44.840
The location is...

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:49.230
If you hurry, you may still make it in time.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:57.350
A man's true form is only revealed once he loses something precious.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:59.850
Goto-san, change of direction.

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:02.200
Please head towards floodgate number seven.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:15.020
Our encounter with Kinoshita-sensei was no coincidence.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.380
It was all <i>his</i> doing.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:18.720
Why would <i>he</i> do that?

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:19.910
I don't know.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:24.150
I just know that he's trying to make me suffer.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.390
I can't help but feel that's his sole reason.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.970
The gate's in sight, Yakumo.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:40.980
Hold it!

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.470
Stop interfering!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:02.630
Let go!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:10.240
I'm not only using Yakumo for his power either!

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:13.390
Let go!

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:39.920
This time... This time, please work...

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:49.760
Yakumo!

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:14.380
Haruka-chan!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:25.080
Don't worry me, you idiot.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:33.230
It seems like you're okay.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:35.590
Yes...

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:41.100
There's something I'd like to try before you take him to the station.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.350
His clinic should suffice.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:45.380
Oh?

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.500
Please call Hata-sensei.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.430
Also, I'd like to ask a favor of Ishii-san.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.360
What are you going to do?

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.360
You'll know soon enough.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:01.870
Why do <i>I</i> have to do this?

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.500
Um... but what exactly are we doing here?

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:25.390
Beats me.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:31.100
Yakumo-kun, is she...

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.400
Yeah.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:36.960
Detective Goto, his eye!

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:38.580
Stay away from me!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:43.060
He can see ghosts with his red eye.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:44.410
R-Really?!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:52.420
Doctor, that woman has been possessed by Ando Takashi's ghost.

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.950
He claims that...

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.430
you were the one who killed him.

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:03.930
A man with two red eyes helped you to see Ayaka-san's ghost, right?

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:10.740
He told me that if I killed a girl with the same age as my daughter, my daughter's soul

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:15.440
would possess the corpse and Ayaka would come back to life.

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:21.320
That explains why the knots tying the bodies to the weights could easily be undone.

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.700
Why did you kill Ando?

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:28.570
I lied when I said he was my junior at my university.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:31.390
That man introduced me to Ando.

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:34.990
Ando's job was to find girls who resembled my daughter.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:36.600
But...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.860
Come on, Doctor.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:43.040
But I just paid you the other day.

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:49.200
If you refuse to pay me, I'll just have to tell the cops everything I know.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:54.110
After all, my only crime was kidnapping girls, as per your instructions.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.210
And although I'll be arrested too,

00:16:57.210 --> 00:17:01.360
it'll be nothing compared to what you, the real murderer, will go through.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:07.470
Besides, if you do get arrested, you'll never see your daughter again.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.880
Fine. I'll pay you.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:22.390
So you slipped drugs into Ando's beer.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.890
I see! So that's what all that money was about!

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:31.610
People who take advantage of a parent's love for their children should die, just like him.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.930
But <i>your</i> victims had parents too.

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:35.650
What?

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:41.910
Whatever your reasons, your actions can't be justified.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.240
Shut up.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:46.680
You were almost killed by your mother.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.410
You'll never understand what it's like for a parent who has lost their child.

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.010
You may be right.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:02.930
However, I do understand what a child who's suffering as a direct consequence of her father's actions feels like.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:08.680
Do you know why all the victims died smiling peacefully?

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:14.350
Ayaka-san's ghost <i>did</i> possess these girls.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.270
Really?!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.280
I met Ayaka-san too.

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:27.300
Ayaka-san's soul entered me.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:30.610
As I felt her enter, I...

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:41.840
She didn't possess the girls because she wanted to return to life,

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:47.800
instead, at the very least, she wanted to remove the fear and suffering from your victims.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:50.310
That's why she possessed those girls.

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:55.770
Yet each time she did, she experienced the fear and pain of death.

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:57.630
Lies!

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:03.330
You're her father, but what you did was equivalent to killing your own daughter over and over again.

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.590
"Please stop doing this."

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:10.540
That's Ayaka-san's one wish.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.280
"Ayaka, please rest in peace."

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:17.870
You're the one who erected that stone memorial, correct?

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:22.050
Please try and remember your feelings from back then.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:25.970
Ayaka...

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.420
Hey, what's wrong?

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:37.290
Where... am I?

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.560
I...

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.140
Ando's ghost has left her.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.580
Hata-sensei, please take care of the rest.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.070
Hey, newbie, help me out.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:48.030
What?

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:50.380
Yes...

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.350
Looks like she's been saved too.

00:19:55.350 --> 00:20:00.090
But why did Ando's ghost leave her?

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:04.890
Either he was satisfied with seeing his killer like this, or...

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:10.610
Or perhaps he finally realized

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:14.920
that it's impossible to return to life even if you possess another's body.

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:25.940
Her ghost is no longer here.

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.110
I see.

00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:30.990
I'm partially responsible for this incident...

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:34.100
The man who put Kinoshita-sensei up to this is...

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:38.440
I don't plan on offering you any comfort,

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:41.760
but there are also people in this world who

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:44.380
continue to live on even after losing their child, without hurting others.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:49.130
Kinoshita lost to the darkness in his own heart.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.400
The darkness in one's heart, eh?

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:00.000
Hey, what's with the gloomy face?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.630
I've loved the occult phenomena ever since I was a child.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:14.160
I believed that you were a psychic detective with special powers who used them to solve difficult cases.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:20.390
What? Wait, was that the reason you were looking at me with such hopeful eyes?

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:25.740
And in the end, it turns out that Saito Yakumo-shi is the one with the psychic powers...

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.780
Oh! So that's what it was!

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.090
Thank goodness!

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:31.620
I was convinced that you...

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:35.180
It's nothing, idiot.

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.970
The truth behind humans is darkness.

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:56.700
You will eventually learn about that darkness.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.710
I will not acknowledge that...

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:02.040
you're my biological father.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.000
Yakumo-kun...

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.490
What's wrong?

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:13.780
Hey, let's go home.

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:21.390
By the way, Mayuko's going to be completely fine, right?

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:22.390
Yeah.

00:22:22.390 --> 00:22:25.550
She only saw the ghost.

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:28.540
But how am I suppose to explain that to her...

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:32.070
I know! Yakumo-kun, can you-

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:33.200
Don't drag me into this any deeper.

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:34.840
Do it yourself.

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:37.210
Don't be like that. Please!

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:39.430
Don't look at me like that. You're making me feel sick.

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:46.420
Yakumo, let's meet again, soon.
